Small.

9
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:24,910
And it is kind of grammar focused, but it's very, very important because you often want to talk about things that don't happen.

10
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:28,210
We're calling these hypotheticals or conditional statements.

11
00:00:28,430 --> 00:00:28,550
Right.

12
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:33,320
And there are different types of hypotheticals or conditional statements.

13
00:00:33,320 --> 00:00:42,060
So today we're going to be looking at the third conditional, which is probably the hardest one because it uses a little bit of a complex grammar structure.

14
00:00:42,060 --> 00:00:46,230
It's complex and we're actually talking about things that did not happen and that will not happen, right?

15
00:00:47,610 --> 00:00:48,080
It's impossible to change.

16
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:52,990
It's impossible to change these because there are things that would have happened in the past but didn't.

17
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:54,450
Wow, that sounds confusing.

18
